Tests for ALB_JACK_BEAT_TRACKING (JackSync beats counted through tempo
changes; see ../beat_tracker.hpp).

Unit tests, no JACK needed::

    make check

Integration test: the real engine against a scripted, Hydrogen-like JACK
timebase master on a private dummy JACK server (no hardware, no effect on
a running rig; the engine's HOME is a temporary directory).  Needs jackd,
oscsend (liblo), python3 with the ``jack`` module, and an engine built
with ALB_SYNC_PULSE_LOG defined, since it reads the pulses from that log::

    ./jack_integration_test.py                   # built with ALB_JACK_BEAT_TRACKING
    ./jack_integration_test.py --expect stock    # built without it

The first passes when every sync pulse lands within 2 samples of the
master's beat through tempo ramps, a relocate while rolling, a stop/start
without a locate, and a stop / locate 0 / start.  The second passes when
the stock code's drift is reproduced.  About 40 s each.  Set SL_BT_KEEP=1
to keep the run's files for inspection.
